                <pb facs="0480" n="378" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg378"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5144: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Munro</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-11-17T09:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">November 17,
                                1927—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>335. The Supreme Court yesterday elected Dr. Joaquin Gomez of Granada president
                    of the National Electoral Board. Gomez is a Progressive and was the candidate of
                    the Liberal magistrates but his selection is also very satisfactory to the
                    Government. He will take office December 1st.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Munro</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
